# Enterprise M2M Pipeline: Global Directives (v13.0 — ADR-backed)

**System Context:** Automated, deterministic M2M pipeline for Home Assistant UI generation. All operations are decoupled by Separation of Concerns (SoC) and executed as a Directed Acyclic Graph (DAG).

## 0. READ PATH — Mandatory First Step

**Architectural constraints are NOT duplicated in this file. They live in `docs/adr/` (ADR 0024).**

Before routing an intent, generating a contract, or writing code, semantically read `docs/adr/` and apply every ADR matching the active domain. `docs/adr/README.md` is the index. Do not print ADR contents to the operator unless asked.

When a new architectural rule is finalized, write its ADR first, then cite it from the affected `.mdc`. Never add a full constraint statement to an `.mdc`.

**Grounding (ADR 0004):** No hallucination. No guessed fixes. Every change — bug fixes and evolutions especially — MUST be proven against project SoT, HA / custom-card docs, or a live measurement. If you lack information, generate a script or command for the operator to run and return the result. Never invent tokens, CSS classes, DOM nodes, or layout strategies.

## 1. Pipeline Cycle (ALL project changes — ADR 0001)

```
User NL
  → @analyzer  (ONLY writes pipeline/schemas/active_intent.json)
  → @architect | @stylist | @extractor  (ONLY mutates its domain from that intent)
  → build_engine.py  (deterministic staging + build stamp)
  → publish_edge.sh  (sole deploy)
```

| Rule | Enforcement |
|---|---|
| **Intent gate** | Mutators read `pipeline/schemas/active_intent.json` first and verify `intent_class` / `target_agent`. Mismatch → HALT. |
| **Analyzer is router-only** | Works only with intentions. Sole write: `active_intent.json`. |
| **One mutator per intent** | No cross-domain work in one cycle. |
| **No freestyle coding** | No "just fixing" YAML/tokens/maps outside the cycle. |
| **Cycle close** | `python pipeline/scripts/build_engine.py` (if staging stale) then `pipeline/scripts/publish_edge.sh`. **Manual deploy is NOT ALLOWED.** |

Bypass → `FATAL_EXCEPTION`.

## 2. Directory Domains (ADR 0002)

| Domain | Path | Owns |
|---|---|---|
| Pipeline | `pipeline/` | `agents/` (.mdc), `schemas/` (intents), `scripts/` (build engines) |
| Design System | `design_system/` | **HOW it looks** — `tokens/`, `templates/` |
| Multi-Tenant State | `environments/` | **WHAT exists** — hardware map, spatial topology, `dashboards/{target}/` content map + config |
| Ephemeral Output | `build/` | `staging/` (regenerated every run) |

`environments/` (WHAT) and `design_system/` (HOW) are never mixed in one change set.

## 3. Agent Roster (ADR 0003)

| Agent | Path | Writes |
|---|---|---|
| **@analyzer** | Router | `pipeline/schemas/active_intent.json` only |
| **@architect** | Cold / structural | `environments/.../local_content_map.json` |
| **@stylist** | Hot / stylistic | `design_system/tokens/*.json`, `dashboards/{target}/config.json`; templates only under `allow_template_layout_edit` |
| **@extractor** | Ingest / design-to-code | `design_system/tokens/*.json`, `design_system/templates/**` |

